    "hash": "41375b5f8fca80f46a9fbd7a80c2ec6ce8cfd2321050c5c69d29b6cb432225e3",
    "summary_one_sentence": "An Internal Affairs officer investigating a protester's critical injury during a chaotic Paris demonstration faces a complex ethical dilemma after discovering the victim is from her hometown.",
    "summary_short": "Internal Affairs officer Stéphanie is assigned to investigate a case involving a young man severely wounded during a tense protest in Paris. Although her initial procedural review finds no evidence of illegal police violence, the investigation becomes deeply personal when she learns the victim shares her hometown roots. As personal connections intersect with her professional responsibilities, Stéphanie is forced to navigate the delicate line between institutional loyalty and uncompromising justice. This poignant crime drama examines the systemic and human complexities behind high-stakes police investigations.",
    "summary_long": "Set amidst the tension of a chaotic street protest in Paris, Case 137 follows Stéphanie, a dedicated officer serving in the police department's Internal Affairs division. When a demonstration turns violent and leaves a young man critically injured, Stéphanie is tasked with determining if excessive force was used by officers on the scene. Her initial examination of body camera footage, witness statements, and official logs reveals no obvious evidence of illegitimate police violence. However, the routine nature of the investigation takes a sharp personal turn when Stéphanie discovers that the victim originates from her small hometown. This unexpected connection forces her to re-examine the case with heightened sensitivity and a deeper awareness of the lives impacted by the incident. As public outcry grows and departmental pressure mounts to close the file quickly, Stéphanie digs deeper into the events of that chaotic night. She finds herself navigating a web of institutional self-preservation, subtle biases, and personal loyalties that test her adherence to the law. Balancing her commitment to the badge with her empathy for a victim tied to her past, Stéphanie remains determined to uncover the full truth. Ultimately, the case forces her to confront the human cost of conflict and the true meaning of justice in a fractured society.",
    "synopsis": "Case 137 is a compelling crime drama centered on Stéphanie, an objective Internal Affairs officer tasked with examining police conduct following a violent Paris demonstration that leaves a young man severely wounded. While early evidence points to lawful police action, Stéphanie's perspective shifts when she realizes the victim hails from her own hometown, turning a standard procedural inquiry into an emotionally charged search for truth amidst systemic pressure and personal conflict.",
